@ref Decision 168/2024, Article 2 (PDF page 1)
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the rules take effect` MEANS YMD 2024 11 15

-- What Article 2 settles, and what it leaves. It says the decision takes effect on 15 November
-- 2024 and REPLACES Decision 53/2024 of 22 May 2024. It does not say which rules govern a
-- contract concluded before that day and still running after it. Decision 53/2024 is another
-- document (encoded by another row, blind to this one), so a contract concluded before the
-- effective date is declined here, by name, rather than answered with these rules.
@ref Decision 168/2024, Article 2: no transitional provision for contracts concluded before 15 November 2024
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a contract concluded before 15 November 2024 is governed by Decision 53/2024, which is not in this encoding` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contract concluded before 15 November 2024 is governed by Decision 53/2024, which is not in this encoding"

-- The gate every chapter's top-level rule passes through first.
@ref Decision 168/2024, Article 2
GIVEN a              IS A TYPE
      `the policy`   IS A `A policy`
      `the answer`   IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`under these rules,` `the policy` `the answer is` `the answer` MEANS
    IF   `the policy`'s `date of conclusion` AT LEAST `the date the rules take effect`
    THEN `the answer`
    ELSE `a contract concluded before 15 November 2024 is governed by Decision 53/2024, which is not in this encoding`

